1
00:00:01,773 --> 00:00:03,173
(Episode 29)

2
00:00:03,343 --> 00:00:05,473
I made a reservation at a great restaurant for lunch.

3
00:00:05,873 --> 00:00:06,913
Sounds good.

4
00:00:07,073 --> 00:00:08,773
- Hello. - Hello.

5
00:01:00,993 --> 00:01:02,463
About Chief Cha...

6
00:01:04,403 --> 00:01:07,303
He's putting everything on the line for this new brand launch.

7
00:01:07,933 --> 00:01:09,333
It's not just a simple brand launch.

8
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:13,243
He's challenging for the flagship brand title at Cheongma.

9
00:01:15,943 --> 00:01:18,243
Does it look that way to you too?

10
00:01:18,843 --> 00:01:19,843
Of course.

11
00:01:20,313 --> 00:01:22,253
I'm looking forward to it because I can feel his ambition,

12
00:01:24,153 --> 00:01:26,383
but it must be a lot of pressure for you,

13
00:01:26,453 --> 00:01:27,953
being on his team.

14
00:01:30,363 --> 00:01:32,423
If the results are good, it's good for me too.

15
00:01:32,863 --> 00:01:35,993
So I really hope this new product gets a good response.

16
00:01:39,263 --> 00:01:40,333
Joo Mi Ran.

17
00:01:41,203 --> 00:01:43,373
No. Joo Ae Sook.

18
00:01:45,243 --> 00:01:48,713
Even her hairstyle's identical. Exactly the same.

19
00:01:49,573 --> 00:01:50,643
Oh, right.

20
00:01:55,053 --> 00:01:57,983
I may not look it, but what's that in the US?

21
00:01:58,183 --> 00:01:59,323
Right, the FBI.

22
00:01:59,383 --> 00:02:01,323
I'm just as good as they are.

23
00:02:02,323 --> 00:02:05,023
I've gathered all this evidence,

24
00:02:05,763 --> 00:02:08,063
and the truth is plain as day.

25
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:11,663
How could she possibly deny this?

26
00:02:15,533 --> 00:02:16,873
Just you wait, Joo Ae Sook.

27
00:02:17,243 --> 00:02:20,413
I'm only asking for five big ones. That's all.

28
00:02:21,873 --> 00:02:24,043
Just have 500,000 dollars ready.

29
00:02:24,413 --> 00:02:25,413
Got it?

30
00:02:29,953 --> 00:02:31,823
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation, PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

31
00:02:31,983 --> 00:02:34,053
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

32
00:02:36,023 --> 00:02:38,723
You went to visit my mother at the hospital the other day.

33
00:02:39,623 --> 00:02:41,333
Yes, how did you know?

34
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:46,163
That colouring book. My mom really liked it.

35
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:50,743
I prepared it in case she got bored in her hospital room.

36
00:02:50,973 --> 00:02:52,043
I'm glad to hear it.

37
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:55,913
Thank you for caring even though you're busy.

38
00:02:57,813 --> 00:02:59,583
Not at all. I enjoyed it too.

39
00:03:00,113 --> 00:03:02,453
I was actually exhausted from having too much work,

40
00:03:02,783 --> 00:03:04,883
but seeing your mother boosted my energy.

41
00:03:06,583 --> 00:03:08,493
I have other colouring books too.

42
00:03:08,793 --> 00:03:10,623
Should I bring them to her?

43
00:03:11,523 --> 00:03:12,793
Yes, that would be great.

44
00:03:13,263 --> 00:03:16,963
Now, write down all the businesses...

45
00:03:17,203 --> 00:03:19,363
or shops you want to run.

46
00:03:19,903 --> 00:03:21,333
You want us to do what?

47
00:03:22,303 --> 00:03:25,442
Why bother making a list of things out of our reach?

48
00:03:25,443 --> 00:03:27,513
Just do as you're told, will you?

49
00:03:27,843 --> 00:03:30,943
Who knows? We might win the lottery someday.

50
00:03:32,213 --> 00:03:34,953
At least buy a lottery ticket before saying that.

51
00:03:36,183 --> 00:03:39,053
What kind of preparation is this without any plan?

52
00:03:39,123 --> 00:03:41,353
That's right. You said it well, Eun Guk.

53
00:03:42,023 --> 00:03:45,123
Why do you think we ended up like this?

54
00:03:45,593 --> 00:03:48,293
It's all because we weren't prepared.

55
00:03:48,633 --> 00:03:51,103
Not having any plans...

56
00:03:52,763 --> 00:03:56,203
is the reason we ended up with nothing at all to our names.

57
00:03:56,843 --> 00:03:58,473
Did you only just realise that, Mom?

58
00:04:00,043 --> 00:04:01,213
Well, then...

59
00:04:03,013 --> 00:04:06,483
A gym. I want to open a really nice gym.

60
00:04:07,083 --> 00:04:09,713
Oh, please. A gym, my foot.

61
00:04:10,323 --> 00:04:13,123
There's a gym on every corner now.

62
00:04:13,523 --> 00:04:14,992
Pick something else.

63
00:04:14,993 --> 00:04:16,763
Then, I...

64
00:04:17,523 --> 00:04:20,463
I think it'd be nice to open a fried chicken place.

65
00:04:20,733 --> 00:04:22,063
You know I love fried chicken.

66
00:04:22,663 --> 00:04:24,833
Seriously?

67
00:04:24,903 --> 00:04:27,733
Every other place is a fried chicken place these days.

68
00:04:28,033 --> 00:04:29,372
Pass. Something else.

69
00:04:29,373 --> 00:04:30,743
Mom!

70
00:04:30,803 --> 00:04:31,873
Grandma?

71
00:04:32,373 --> 00:04:33,443
Forget it.

72
00:04:33,873 --> 00:04:36,043
Preparing ahead, my foot. What nonsense.

73
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,143
Let's just live the way we always have.

74
00:04:39,213 --> 00:04:40,213
Unbelievable.

75
00:04:42,653 --> 00:04:44,553
Wait a minute.

76
00:04:44,623 --> 00:04:46,853
- What did I expect? - Hold on.

77
00:04:47,093 --> 00:04:49,053
Why am I the only one who got hit?

78
00:04:49,953 --> 00:04:52,193
- You said a fried chicken place. - How's a gym any better?

79
00:04:53,223 --> 00:04:54,693
There's a reason she didn't hit me too.

80
00:05:01,273 --> 00:05:02,633
Is that a lunch box?

81
00:05:03,643 --> 00:05:04,843
Are we going on a picnic?

82
00:05:05,303 --> 00:05:08,373
No, not a picnic. It's just for us to eat.

83
00:05:09,673 --> 00:05:11,783
Why are you packing food when it's just for us?

84
00:05:13,013 --> 00:05:14,113
Is it for Uncle?

85
00:05:14,383 --> 00:05:15,413
What?

86
00:05:15,783 --> 00:05:17,753
Are you going to take it to Uncle's office?

87
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:22,923
No, it's not that.

88
00:05:24,193 --> 00:05:27,192
I just thought we could share it with others.

89
00:05:27,193 --> 00:05:28,233
Sounds good.

90
00:05:28,863 --> 00:05:30,863
Then let's pack some for Uncle Jokbal too.

91
00:05:31,703 --> 00:05:34,533
You know he has a huge appetite.

92
00:05:36,133 --> 00:05:37,573
Sure, let's do that.

93
00:05:49,313 --> 00:05:50,323
Oh, my.

94
00:05:50,683 --> 00:05:51,683
Pretty, right?

95
00:05:51,983 --> 00:05:52,983
It is.

96
00:05:54,023 --> 00:05:57,263
I coloured this with the nice lady.

97
00:05:57,693 --> 00:05:59,963
She's even good at colouring.

98
00:06:01,863 --> 00:06:03,633
You like that nice lady that much, Mom?

99
00:06:04,933 --> 00:06:09,503
Yes, the nice lady is pretty and kind.

100
00:06:10,543 --> 00:06:12,973
And she likes me.

101
00:06:14,543 --> 00:06:16,613
Hae Ra likes you just as much.

102
00:06:18,283 --> 00:06:19,943
Hae Ra doesn't like me.

103
00:06:21,213 --> 00:06:23,823
You're wrong. She may complain a little,

104
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:25,923
but she likes you a lot, too.

105
00:06:26,823 --> 00:06:30,293
I'm telling you, she doesn't. Hae Ra doesn't like me.

106
00:06:32,393 --> 00:06:33,593
Mom, are you angry?

107
00:06:34,993 --> 00:06:37,163
Yes, I'm angry.

108
00:06:38,933 --> 00:06:40,273
I know...

109
00:06:40,603 --> 00:06:44,003
who really likes me and who doesn't.

110
00:06:44,043 --> 00:06:45,343
I can tell.

111
00:06:46,673 --> 00:06:47,773
Can you really tell?

112
00:06:48,743 --> 00:06:50,113
Of course.

113
00:06:50,813 --> 00:06:54,553
The nice lady genuinely likes me.

114
00:06:55,553 --> 00:06:57,553
I can tell by looking at her eyes.

115
00:06:57,983 --> 00:06:59,683
The nice lady's eyes...

116
00:07:00,393 --> 00:07:03,723
She has such warm eyes when she looks at me.

117
00:07:10,963 --> 00:07:12,963
(Cheongma)

118
00:07:13,973 --> 00:07:15,332
Right. I heard buyers...

119
00:07:15,333 --> 00:07:17,743
had great things to say about the new product.

120
00:07:18,243 --> 00:07:19,273
Yes, sir.

121
00:07:19,743 --> 00:07:22,213
The initial run alone won't be enough to meet demand.

122
00:07:22,713 --> 00:07:24,983
We're expanding production now.

123
00:07:25,483 --> 00:07:26,613
Good.

124
00:07:27,613 --> 00:07:28,613
Dad.

125
00:07:28,683 --> 00:07:30,823
Once the store's opening ceremony wraps up smoothly,

126
00:07:31,253 --> 00:07:32,522
why don't Seok Jin and I...

127
00:07:32,523 --> 00:07:34,823
start planning the wedding?

128
00:07:35,293 --> 00:07:36,653
I'm not sure.

129
00:07:37,023 --> 00:07:39,223
I think it's still a bit premature.

130
00:07:40,363 --> 00:07:42,133
Chief Cha, what do you think?

131
00:07:42,393 --> 00:07:45,233
You're not going to be satisfied with just the domestic business.

132
00:07:45,663 --> 00:07:48,403
Settling into the domestic market is only the beginning.

133
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:53,173
Making Shoejoy a global brand is the ultimate goal.

134
00:07:54,443 --> 00:07:55,513
As it should be.

135
00:07:56,273 --> 00:08:00,213
I think people aren't so different from businesses.

136
00:08:01,753 --> 00:08:04,123
Just like our investment in this new brand,

137
00:08:04,683 --> 00:08:05,823
Cheongma has invested...

138
00:08:06,183 --> 00:08:09,153
a significant amount of value in you.

139
00:08:09,953 --> 00:08:11,422
Everything from your studies abroad...

140
00:08:11,423 --> 00:08:13,293
to your current role as Planning Director...

141
00:08:14,533 --> 00:08:16,193
has been an investment.

142
00:08:16,963 --> 00:08:20,603
We're just starting to break even,

143
00:08:21,033 --> 00:08:22,033
and you want to get married?

144
00:08:22,733 --> 00:08:26,273
We need to get back at least 3 to 4 times what we put in.

145
00:08:26,343 --> 00:08:28,313
That's the only way it's worth our while.

146
00:08:29,573 --> 00:08:32,383
Dad, Seok Jin is not a stock.

147
00:08:32,443 --> 00:08:33,783
What do you mean by return?

148
00:08:34,553 --> 00:08:36,853
I will miss my chance to marry.

149
00:08:36,953 --> 00:08:37,983
Is that so?

150
00:08:39,253 --> 00:08:40,283
If you're in such a hurry,

151
00:08:41,053 --> 00:08:43,793
you should look for another man to marry.

152
00:08:44,523 --> 00:08:45,563
Dad!

153
00:08:54,203 --> 00:08:55,403
This is so frustrating.

154
00:08:55,873 --> 00:08:58,103
Why does Dad keep delaying our wedding?

155
00:08:58,543 --> 00:09:01,913
He said he'd let us get married if the new brand launch went well,

156
00:09:02,273 --> 00:09:03,543
but now he's talking about expanding globally?

157
00:09:04,083 --> 00:09:06,283
Why does he keep changing his mind?

158
00:09:07,053 --> 00:09:08,683
I'm with him on this one.

159
00:09:08,883 --> 00:09:09,883
Really?

160
00:09:10,353 --> 00:09:12,883
- You are? - I need to establish...

161
00:09:13,123 --> 00:09:16,623
the brand on my own so there will not be any gossip.

162
00:09:17,393 --> 00:09:18,393
To do that,

163
00:09:19,363 --> 00:09:20,993
dominating the domestic market isn't enough.

164
00:09:21,633 --> 00:09:24,733
If I wait that long, I'll be an old woman.

165
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:28,433
I'm in my prime right now, you know.

166
00:09:31,703 --> 00:09:32,703
But...

167
00:09:32,843 --> 00:09:35,513
this prime will only last a few more years.

168
00:09:38,583 --> 00:09:40,753
You have to marry me before my prime is over, okay?

169
00:09:41,153 --> 00:09:42,853
- Got it? - Got it.

170
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,083
Oh, right.

171
00:09:45,253 --> 00:09:46,653
You didn't forget about the gathering today, did you?

172
00:09:49,993 --> 00:09:51,323
Do I really have to go to that?

173
00:09:52,093 --> 00:09:54,563
Of course. I already said you were coming.

174
00:09:56,393 --> 00:09:59,333
You know how important my dad thinks it is.

175
00:09:59,403 --> 00:10:01,203
It's all about networking.

176
00:10:02,873 --> 00:10:04,273
If you're going to marry me,

177
00:10:04,343 --> 00:10:06,143
you need to get used to those kinds of gatherings.

178
00:10:08,773 --> 00:10:09,813
By the way,

179
00:10:10,983 --> 00:10:12,683
you're not wearing that, right?

180
00:10:13,283 --> 00:10:16,853
Reviewing the paperwork isn't going to be enough.

181
00:10:17,883 --> 00:10:21,553
I think a field evaluation is necessary.

182
00:10:21,793 --> 00:10:23,393
What do you think, Eun Seol?

183
00:10:24,163 --> 00:10:26,263
I think a field evaluation is needed too.

184
00:10:26,593 --> 00:10:28,433
Even though I've experienced it myself,

185
00:10:28,493 --> 00:10:30,733
I didn't complete every program.

186
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:32,833
Depending on the inmates' needs,

187
00:10:32,903 --> 00:10:34,873
the programs are all run differently.

188
00:10:36,203 --> 00:10:39,203
Conducting an evaluation while the scholarship program...

189
00:10:39,503 --> 00:10:40,773
isn't finalised yet...

190
00:10:40,843 --> 00:10:43,013
could harm the company's reputation.

191
00:10:44,213 --> 00:10:47,043
Especially since we are about to launch a new brand.

192
00:10:47,513 --> 00:10:50,753
Director Joo. The Cheongma Scholarship Foundation...

193
00:10:51,453 --> 00:10:54,593
isn't a promotional prop for Cheongma Group.

194
00:10:56,023 --> 00:10:58,163
Even if the rest of the group focuses on...

195
00:10:58,223 --> 00:11:00,563
immediate profits and business acumen,

196
00:11:00,763 --> 00:11:04,503
our scholarship foundation at least needs to stay true...

197
00:11:04,903 --> 00:11:07,803
to its core philosophy and social values.

198
00:11:10,903 --> 00:11:14,313
So be sure to wrap everything up before the brand launch.

199
00:11:14,873 --> 00:11:15,873
Hold on.

200
00:11:15,913 --> 00:11:19,743
Eun Seol, why don't we pick a date for the field evaluation?

201
00:11:19,883 --> 00:11:22,153
Sure, I'll check my schedule.

202
00:11:22,713 --> 00:11:25,823
Good. I have a good feeling about this.

203
00:11:29,693 --> 00:11:33,423
What? They're going to a prison for a field evaluation?

204
00:11:34,093 --> 00:11:37,303
Yes. The Chairman's being really stubborn,

205
00:11:37,833 --> 00:11:40,833
and Ko Eun Seol is also actively expressing her intentions,

206
00:11:41,073 --> 00:11:42,703
so it wasn't easy to stop them.

207
00:11:44,243 --> 00:11:47,743
I've always had reservations about Ko Eun Seol.

208
00:11:49,313 --> 00:11:52,983
You can't ignore the environment someone was born and raised in.

209
00:11:53,613 --> 00:11:56,013
A leopard can't change its spots.

210
00:11:56,653 --> 00:11:59,053
Look at what happened between her and Hae Ra back in high school.

211
00:11:59,683 --> 00:12:01,093
Framed or not,

212
00:12:01,553 --> 00:12:04,123
it was still a charge for killing her own mother.

213
00:12:04,993 --> 00:12:07,332
She managed to survive in such a harsh, unforgiving environment...

214
00:12:07,333 --> 00:12:08,633
for a full ten years.

215
00:12:09,533 --> 00:12:12,303
Who knows what someone like her is secretly harbouring?

216
00:12:14,203 --> 00:12:15,403
To be honest,

217
00:12:15,773 --> 00:12:19,003
that part about her has always bothered me as well.

218
00:12:20,073 --> 00:12:21,273
Anyway, my wife...

219
00:12:22,073 --> 00:12:24,513
Her main flaw is that she's far too trusting.

220
00:12:25,713 --> 00:12:28,183
Maybe it's because she had an easy life growing up,

221
00:12:28,253 --> 00:12:30,183
but she's never cautious enough.

222
00:12:31,583 --> 00:12:34,423
Should I call it being naive?

223
00:12:36,623 --> 00:12:38,523
To ease your concerns,

224
00:12:38,593 --> 00:12:40,793
I'll support her closely by her side, sir.

225
00:12:42,063 --> 00:12:43,933
Good. By the way,

226
00:12:44,533 --> 00:12:47,933
we need to bring the foundation board members in quietly...

227
00:12:48,003 --> 00:12:49,333
and pull a few strings.

228
00:12:50,133 --> 00:12:52,573
Set things up beforehand...

229
00:12:53,003 --> 00:12:55,073
so that when it goes to a board vote,

230
00:12:55,243 --> 00:12:56,843
the opposition wins by a landslide.

231
00:12:57,643 --> 00:13:00,883
Understood, I'll reach out to the board members privately.

232
00:13:03,653 --> 00:13:05,383
Wait. What is all this?

233
00:13:06,123 --> 00:13:08,793
I brought leftovers from when I packed Hyun Jae's lunch yesterday.

234
00:13:10,093 --> 00:13:13,323
How much did you make to have this much left over?

235
00:13:14,563 --> 00:13:17,193
I'm really bad at portion control.

236
00:13:19,133 --> 00:13:21,573
Working under a boss with magic hands for cooking...

237
00:13:21,933 --> 00:13:23,503
comes with great perks like this.

238
00:13:30,813 --> 00:13:31,813
Boss,

239
00:13:31,883 --> 00:13:34,213
I'll get back to this after my delivery run.

240
00:13:35,153 --> 00:13:36,283
Hurry back then.

241
00:13:47,463 --> 00:13:48,493
Hello, ma'am.

242
00:13:49,533 --> 00:13:51,633
Oh my, what is all this?

243
00:13:55,803 --> 00:13:59,003
Wait. Did you pack all this for Eun Guk?

244
00:14:00,073 --> 00:14:01,113
Gosh, no.

245
00:14:06,213 --> 00:14:07,683
It's not bad at all.

246
00:14:10,883 --> 00:14:12,523
Please slow down.

247
00:14:13,123 --> 00:14:14,153
You see,

248
00:14:14,223 --> 00:14:16,523
I really need the energy from food right now.

249
00:14:16,593 --> 00:14:19,093
I have to eat well to handle a big event.

250
00:14:21,893 --> 00:14:24,633
Then you should eat it later with your precious grandson.

251
00:14:27,873 --> 00:14:29,903
See? I knew it.

252
00:14:30,973 --> 00:14:33,243
You are trying to fatten up Eun Guk...

253
00:14:33,303 --> 00:14:35,143
so you can snatch him up, right?

254
00:14:35,873 --> 00:14:37,273
Of course not!

255
00:14:37,843 --> 00:14:39,783
Don't you dare set your sights on him.

256
00:14:40,113 --> 00:14:42,713
Our family might be in this state right now,

257
00:14:43,313 --> 00:14:46,583
but we were a wealthy family for generations...

258
00:14:46,983 --> 00:14:49,093
and a family that everyone looked up to.

259
00:14:49,723 --> 00:14:52,323
Our Eun Guk is the precious only son...

260
00:14:52,923 --> 00:14:56,993
of the third generation in such a family.

261
00:14:57,293 --> 00:14:59,003
You should know your place.

262
00:14:59,833 --> 00:15:01,533
Yes, I see.

263
00:15:04,773 --> 00:15:05,843
It's good.

264
00:15:13,213 --> 00:15:14,213
Right.

265
00:15:14,983 --> 00:15:17,423
He isn't just your typical bad news.

266
00:15:17,853 --> 00:15:20,023
Everything about him smells rotten.

267
00:15:20,323 --> 00:15:21,953
He gambles, steals,

268
00:15:22,893 --> 00:15:25,223
and to top it off, he's a total womanizer.

269
00:15:25,663 --> 00:15:27,223
The guy is pure trash.

270
00:15:28,133 --> 00:15:29,833
Where did you say he was again?

271
00:15:30,133 --> 00:15:33,933
Well, he doesn't really keep a routine,

272
00:15:34,003 --> 00:15:36,133
so I can't tell you exactly where he's at.

273
00:15:36,703 --> 00:15:39,573
Either way, I think he's somewhere around Seoul.

274
00:15:40,543 --> 00:15:41,743
Seoul?

275
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:44,843
He used to hang around Chungcheong Province,

276
00:15:45,883 --> 00:15:48,553
but lately he's been floating around Seoul.

277
00:15:51,923 --> 00:15:55,793
(Kang Do Hyun, Yoon Tae Min, Choi Jun Hwan, Choi Jin Ho)

278
00:15:55,853 --> 00:15:58,022
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

279
00:15:58,023 --> 00:15:59,923
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

280
00:16:10,533 --> 00:16:11,773
Director, it's me.

281
00:16:13,303 --> 00:16:14,543
Things are urgent,

282
00:16:15,543 --> 00:16:17,373
so we need to move up the interview dates.

283
00:16:18,583 --> 00:16:19,583
Yes, I'll do that.

284
00:16:25,523 --> 00:16:26,983
I need to hire someone quickly...

285
00:16:27,823 --> 00:16:29,693
and find that scum An Guk Cheol first.

286
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:38,733
Come in.

287
00:16:45,003 --> 00:16:46,903
Please give this to your mother.

288
00:16:47,273 --> 00:16:49,813
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

289
00:16:49,873 --> 00:16:50,883
Thanks.

290
00:16:52,113 --> 00:16:54,683
The drawing's a bit intricate, so it won't be easy,

291
00:16:54,753 --> 00:16:56,583
but your mother will still like it.

292
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:00,023
I think you and my mom have similar tastes.

293
00:17:01,423 --> 00:17:03,353
I know. I think so too.

294
00:17:10,593 --> 00:17:11,633
That ring.

295
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:14,703
You got matching ones with Hae Ra, right?

296
00:17:18,243 --> 00:17:19,403
That ring...

297
00:17:22,543 --> 00:17:25,183
It isn't very pretty. Could you not wear it?

298
00:17:31,083 --> 00:17:32,683
I'm just saying.

299
00:17:46,803 --> 00:17:48,803
Slow down, or it's going to hit you fast.

300
00:17:49,233 --> 00:17:51,443
- Why are you laughing? - Cha Seok Jin!

301
00:17:53,403 --> 00:17:55,513
Hey, it's been a while.

302
00:17:59,183 --> 00:18:00,383
Sure, it's been a while.

303
00:18:01,913 --> 00:18:04,783
Look at you, Hae Ra. Stunning as always.

304
00:18:04,983 --> 00:18:06,023
Thank you.

305
00:18:07,523 --> 00:18:08,753
You haven't changed much either.

306
00:18:10,023 --> 00:18:11,263
Another new partner?

307
00:18:12,063 --> 00:18:13,563
Just how many women are you seeing?

308
00:18:13,693 --> 00:18:15,293
That takes talent to pull off.

309
00:18:16,093 --> 00:18:17,293
Hey, it's Si Won.

310
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:19,533
- Seok Jin, just a second. - Sure.

311
00:18:24,773 --> 00:18:27,873
You know, you keep looking better and better.

312
00:18:28,473 --> 00:18:30,373
Seriously though, how much did all this cost?

313
00:18:31,783 --> 00:18:33,343
Looks like Hae Ra treated you well.

314
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:38,723
Sure. Hae Ra and the CEO treat me pretty good.

315
00:18:38,983 --> 00:18:41,053
Oh, really? Even the CEO?

316
00:18:42,153 --> 00:18:44,463
Cheongma treats their son-in-law very well.

317
00:18:45,293 --> 00:18:47,733
Hey, if I'd known it'd turn out like this,

318
00:18:47,993 --> 00:18:49,993
I would've made an effort with Hae Ra.

319
00:18:51,563 --> 00:18:53,903
Come on. Like you ever had a chance.

320
00:18:54,503 --> 00:18:56,733
Hae Ra's liked Seok Jin for ages.

321
00:18:57,403 --> 00:18:58,743
Ever since high school,

322
00:18:59,173 --> 00:19:01,273
- Hae Ra's only had eyes for him. - Darn.

323
00:19:02,373 --> 00:19:04,513
I should've been pathetic like a certain someone.

324
00:19:06,543 --> 00:19:09,213
As you know, pathetic is her type.

325
00:19:13,883 --> 00:19:15,193
How's business going?

326
00:19:18,163 --> 00:19:20,993
I'm just getting by, I suppose.

327
00:19:21,963 --> 00:19:22,993
Really?

328
00:19:24,093 --> 00:19:25,133
From what I heard,

329
00:19:25,703 --> 00:19:29,103
your main bank rejected your loan extension,

330
00:19:29,703 --> 00:19:32,043
and your contract with the main distributor was blocked.

331
00:19:34,913 --> 00:19:35,913
Tell me if you're struggling.

332
00:19:37,213 --> 00:19:39,243
I'll put in a good word with the CEO.

333
00:19:49,253 --> 00:19:51,493
Darn it, Cha Seok Jin.

334
00:19:53,993 --> 00:19:56,193
Why do you get so twisted whenever you see him?

335
00:19:56,663 --> 00:19:58,063
It's not like you get anything out of it.

336
00:19:58,333 --> 00:20:00,763
He just acts like he's so high and mighty.

337
00:20:01,903 --> 00:20:04,443
He thinks he's something special just because he's dating Hae Ra.

338
00:20:05,443 --> 00:20:06,673
At the end of the day,

339
00:20:06,843 --> 00:20:09,373
he's just a loyal dog on Cheongma's leash.

340
00:20:10,543 --> 00:20:14,453
I heard the brand he just launched is doing well, too.

341
00:20:14,713 --> 00:20:16,983
That's all just for show, you idiot.

342
00:20:17,613 --> 00:20:19,822
He's a son-in-law in name only,

343
00:20:19,823 --> 00:20:22,493
while they dump all of Cheongma's dirty work on him.

344
00:20:23,323 --> 00:20:26,293
Hey, even mutts don't eat just any dog food these days.

345
00:20:27,763 --> 00:20:31,433
That work of his is just like premium dog food.

346
00:20:33,333 --> 00:20:35,403
People who are born with a servile mindset...

347
00:20:35,473 --> 00:20:37,173
are just beyond saving.

348
00:20:49,153 --> 00:20:50,283
Are you busy?

349
00:20:51,053 --> 00:20:52,783
No, I'm free to talk.

350
00:20:53,383 --> 00:20:54,953
Did you have something to say?

351
00:20:55,493 --> 00:20:57,993
No, not really.

352
00:20:59,423 --> 00:21:02,293
Well, your dad mentioned...

353
00:21:02,693 --> 00:21:06,003
that you're planning to look for your biological mother eventually.

354
00:21:07,033 --> 00:21:09,173
Yes, I should.

355
00:21:10,773 --> 00:21:11,843
I should at least try to find her.

356
00:21:12,973 --> 00:21:14,643
You're curious about her too, right?

357
00:21:15,343 --> 00:21:18,213
Yes. She might not compare to Mom,

358
00:21:18,343 --> 00:21:20,913
but she's still my biological mother,

359
00:21:21,313 --> 00:21:23,013
so I've always felt grateful to her.

360
00:21:23,883 --> 00:21:25,423
That's something I've never forgotten.

361
00:21:26,583 --> 00:21:27,723
Right, okay then.

362
00:21:29,493 --> 00:21:31,393
Even if you've never seen her face,

363
00:21:31,763 --> 00:21:33,723
she's still the one who brought you into this world,

364
00:21:34,833 --> 00:21:37,363
so the two of you...

365
00:21:37,763 --> 00:21:39,603
ought to meet at least once.

366
00:21:40,203 --> 00:21:43,203
You share the same blood, after all.

367
00:21:43,933 --> 00:21:44,943
What?

368
00:21:45,743 --> 00:21:47,773
Never mind. Get back to work.

369
00:21:49,413 --> 00:21:50,943
Right. Good night.

370
00:21:51,113 --> 00:21:52,583
Sure, you too.

371
00:22:04,923 --> 00:22:06,223
Just you wait, Joo Ae Sook.

372
00:22:06,793 --> 00:22:09,793
I'll soon bring you your biological daughter.

373
00:22:11,093 --> 00:22:12,803
For our Eun Seol,

374
00:22:13,033 --> 00:22:15,373
for the first and final time,

375
00:22:15,433 --> 00:22:18,203
I need to step up and be a proper grandmother.

376
00:22:42,633 --> 00:22:43,733
Cheongma has invested...

377
00:22:44,093 --> 00:22:47,063
a significant amount of value in you.

378
00:22:47,703 --> 00:22:51,072
We need to get back at least 3 to 4 times what we put in.

379
00:22:51,073 --> 00:22:53,203
That's the only way it's worth our while.

380
00:22:53,703 --> 00:22:55,943
He's a son-in-law in name only,

381
00:22:56,013 --> 00:22:59,383
while they dump all of Cheongma's dirty work on him.

382
00:22:59,443 --> 00:23:02,453
Hey, even mutts don't eat just any dog food these days.

383
00:23:03,813 --> 00:23:07,483
That work of his is just like premium dog food.

384
00:23:09,453 --> 00:23:11,523
People who are born with a servile mindset...

385
00:23:11,593 --> 00:23:13,223
are just beyond saving.

386
00:23:21,163 --> 00:23:24,133
(10 years ago)

387
00:23:24,203 --> 00:23:26,443
It's a study abroad program hosted by the Ministry of Education,

388
00:23:26,943 --> 00:23:28,343
and the terms look ideal for you.

389
00:23:34,513 --> 00:23:35,783
Prepare well and apply for it.

390
00:23:37,253 --> 00:23:38,723
Since it's backed by the ministry,

391
00:23:39,253 --> 00:23:41,083
you'll likely earn extra points on your record.

392
00:23:42,493 --> 00:23:43,493
Right.

393
00:23:43,793 --> 00:23:45,093
- Thank you. - Sure.

394
00:24:05,283 --> 00:24:10,253
(2016 Global Youth Study Abroad Program)

395
00:24:14,553 --> 00:24:15,553
Seriously.

396
00:24:16,793 --> 00:24:18,563
Hey, Cha Seok Jin.

397
00:24:19,523 --> 00:24:20,523
Have you been studying?

398
00:24:24,133 --> 00:24:25,133
Hey.

399
00:24:27,433 --> 00:24:29,073
Take it easy, man.

400
00:24:31,843 --> 00:24:33,543
Just relax a bit.

401
00:24:34,613 --> 00:24:37,413
You're going to suffer for nothing if you try that hard.

402
00:24:39,013 --> 00:24:40,013
What do you mean by that?

403
00:24:40,443 --> 00:24:43,483
Never mind. You just keep working hard, okay?

404
00:24:44,213 --> 00:24:46,423
That way, it'll be more fun to stab you in the back later.

405
00:24:53,093 --> 00:24:54,263
I'm sorry, Seok Jin.

406
00:24:55,033 --> 00:24:57,233
Min Jae Seong in our class got chosen...

407
00:24:57,733 --> 00:25:00,063
for that government overseas program.

408
00:25:02,133 --> 00:25:04,473
Jae Seong can study overseas anytime he wants,

409
00:25:05,343 --> 00:25:06,403
but you know how it is.

410
00:25:07,143 --> 00:25:09,273
This program boosts your student record.

411
00:25:12,383 --> 00:25:13,413
I'm sure you know...

412
00:25:13,643 --> 00:25:15,613
that his father is an assemblyman.

413
00:25:48,783 --> 00:25:50,183
Seok Jin, what do we do?

414
00:25:50,613 --> 00:25:52,123
Your mom's missing.

415
00:25:53,323 --> 00:25:56,153
She kept going on about sending you to the US.

416
00:26:08,303 --> 00:26:09,433
Hey!

417
00:26:10,373 --> 00:26:13,903
How are you not done with this yet?

418
00:26:14,873 --> 00:26:17,143
I'm sorry. I'll clean it up quickly.

419
00:26:17,373 --> 00:26:19,343
- I'm sorry. - Hold on.

420
00:26:19,683 --> 00:26:21,453
I hired just anyone because I was in a rush,

421
00:26:22,153 --> 00:26:24,013
but are you slow or something?

422
00:26:24,083 --> 00:26:26,853
Gosh, I'm so sorry.

423
00:26:30,093 --> 00:26:31,153
Hey.

424
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:33,363
I'm not paying you today,

425
00:26:33,663 --> 00:26:35,733
so just know that and hurry up and clean.

426
00:26:36,293 --> 00:26:38,103
I'm so sorry.

427
00:26:53,983 --> 00:26:54,983
Get up.

428
00:26:59,883 --> 00:27:01,453
Hey, Mr. Seok Jin.

429
00:27:03,123 --> 00:27:04,193
Get up, Mom.

430
00:27:04,993 --> 00:27:07,593
No. I have to clean all this...

431
00:27:07,993 --> 00:27:11,163
and get paid so I can send you to the US.

432
00:27:14,663 --> 00:27:16,603
Please, just get up!

433
00:27:24,073 --> 00:27:25,083
Why...

434
00:27:26,843 --> 00:27:30,813
Why are you suddenly yelling at me?

435
00:27:32,283 --> 00:27:33,823
You're scaring me.

436
00:27:34,523 --> 00:27:36,053
Mom, please.

437
00:27:47,303 --> 00:27:48,473
Come on.

438
00:27:49,133 --> 00:27:50,533
Mr. Seok Jin...

439
00:27:51,103 --> 00:27:53,442
Hey, you can't just leave!

440
00:27:53,443 --> 00:27:56,343
You have to clean this up first. Seriously?

441
00:27:56,943 --> 00:28:00,413
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation, Major Programs)

442
00:28:00,483 --> 00:28:02,083
- Seok Jin. - Yes?

443
00:28:02,883 --> 00:28:04,983
The scholarship foundation directors recommended you.

444
00:28:06,123 --> 00:28:07,923
You'll be able to go this time.

445
00:28:19,063 --> 00:28:20,763
You want me to take my mother too?

446
00:28:22,273 --> 00:28:25,243
I thought it'd be good for So Yeon to get treatment in the US too.

447
00:28:28,513 --> 00:28:31,843
So Yeon, you'd like to go to the US with Seok Jin, right?

448
00:28:33,613 --> 00:28:36,853
As long as I'm with Seok Jin, I'll be happy anywhere.

449
00:28:41,183 --> 00:28:42,192
All done.

450
00:28:42,193 --> 00:28:45,563
Mr. Seok Jin, where are we going tomorrow?

451
00:28:46,763 --> 00:28:48,233
Someplace nice.

452
00:28:48,863 --> 00:28:51,733
Then are we never coming back here?

453
00:28:52,163 --> 00:28:53,833
No, we have to come back.

454
00:28:55,773 --> 00:28:57,803
I'm going to make it big and return.

455
00:29:49,123 --> 00:29:50,123
Goodness.

456
00:29:54,023 --> 00:29:55,033
Just a second.

457
00:29:55,863 --> 00:29:57,193
Excuse me, but where are you going?

458
00:29:57,663 --> 00:29:58,663
Me?

459
00:29:59,263 --> 00:30:01,973
Well, Joo Ae Sook... No, wait.

460
00:30:02,733 --> 00:30:04,503
I'm here to see Joo Mi Ran.

461
00:30:04,703 --> 00:30:05,843
Director Joo?

462
00:30:06,243 --> 00:30:07,672
Do you have an appointment?

463
00:30:07,673 --> 00:30:09,573
No, I don't have one,

464
00:30:10,273 --> 00:30:12,713
but I'm a very important guest.

465
00:30:13,413 --> 00:30:15,453
Anyway, where's her office?

466
00:30:15,513 --> 00:30:17,083
Let me look into this.

467
00:30:39,143 --> 00:30:40,503
Isn't she Joo Mi Ran?

468
00:30:41,073 --> 00:30:42,113
Joo Mi Ran!

469
00:30:43,543 --> 00:30:45,313
I mean, Joo Ae Sook!

470
00:30:49,813 --> 00:30:54,183
(Episode 30 will air on Monday, October 5 at 7:50pm.)

471
00:31:13,743 --> 00:31:17,443
(A Trap Called Desire)

472
00:31:17,543 --> 00:31:19,283
Right here. I'm her man.

473
00:31:19,343 --> 00:31:21,853
- Baby. - Of all the babies, did Hee Jung...

474
00:31:21,913 --> 00:31:24,753
have to bring home one that was never loved?

475
00:31:24,813 --> 00:31:28,593
Did your superior say something to you?

476
00:31:28,853 --> 00:31:30,052
A friend...

477
00:31:30,053 --> 00:31:32,463
Why do you dread Dad's memorial service every year?

478
00:31:32,523 --> 00:31:35,163
I told you. Just think of it like a birthday.

479
00:31:35,233 --> 00:31:37,732
Did you get the medicine for me? Thank you, Ae Sook.

480
00:31:37,733 --> 00:31:40,803
You sure stuffed yourself with a lot, didn't you?

481
00:31:41,363 --> 00:31:43,573
No wonder your stomach is bursting.

482
00:31:43,803 --> 00:31:46,842
Aren't you seeing anyone, Eun Seol?

483
00:31:46,843 --> 00:31:48,243
Is there somebody you like?

484
00:31:48,273 --> 00:31:49,973
Could it be Chief Cha by any chance?
